From: Felipe Bonetto <felipesensbonetto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fx2_ll: clear bulk endpoint halts after claim on macOS

On macOS, the XPCU's bulk endpoints (0x02 OUT, 0x86 IN) can come up
in a halted state after the device re-enumerates following firmware
load. The XPCU driver's first JTAG control transfer (GPIO_TRANSFER)
expects the bulk endpoints to be ready to accept data immediately
after; if they're halted, the FX2 firmware blocks waiting on stalled
pipes and never ACKs the control transfer, manifesting as
LIBUSB_ERROR_TIMEOUT on what should be a fast vendor command.

libusb_clear_halt is a no-op on a healthy endpoint, so it's safe to
issue unconditionally for the XPCU's known endpoints.

--- a/src/fx2_ll.cpp
+++ b/src/fx2_ll.cpp
@@ -80,6 +80,13 @@
 		libusb_exit(usb_ctx);
 		throw std::runtime_error("claim interface failed");
 	}
+	/* macOS: bulk endpoints can come up halted after re-enumeration
+	 * (post firmware-load). Clear them so the first bulk transfer
+	 * doesn't hit a stalled pipe. clear_halt is harmless on a healthy
+	 * endpoint, so we do it unconditionally for the XPCU's known
+	 * endpoints (0x02 OUT, 0x86 IN). Ignore errors. */
+	libusb_clear_halt(dev_handle, 0x02);
+	libusb_clear_halt(dev_handle, 0x86);
 }
 
 bool FX2_ll::set_interface_alt_setting(const int if_num, const int alt_setting)
